welcome back to new rockstars i'm  whitney van laningham and one of my  biggest questions after seeing love and  thunder is about that post-credits scene  you know where daddy zeus swears  vengeance on thor for stabbing him and  ruining his orgy but what are zeus's  plans to get back at the god of thunder  who besides hercules will aid in his  attempt to teach thor and new asgard a  lesson in respecting your horny  shirtless elders and how exactly will  this plot tie in with the future of the  mcu in the post-credits scene zeus tells  his zeus and his son hercules quote they  beg for your mercy without them knowing  if you're actually listening now when  they look to the sky they don't ask us  for lightning they don't ask for rain  they just want to see one of their  so-called superheroes when did we become  the joke no no more they will fear us  again when thor odinson falls from the  sky clearly the surface level  implication here is that zeus is  embarrassed by being shown up by thor to  roughly quote the khan's favorite rock  star bon jovi shut through the heart and  those two blame he gives gods a bad name  so to sue this fragile olympian ego zeus  is sending hercules out on a quest to  publicly humiliate thor and his  superhero friends in front of mortals to  re-establish the gods as beings to be  feared and worshipped although he didn't  get much more from the mcu's hercules  than a classic extremely rough roy kent  responds to daddy zeus's plan to pick up  where gore left off we do know a lot  about his character from the comics back  in 1986's journey into mystery annual  number one thor and hercules met when  thor crashed through the entrance to  olympus and started wrestling with the  son of zeus many of thor and herc's  early storylines depicted the two of  them brawling for panels upon panels  mostly to showcase the fact that their  strengths and powers were so equally  matched not only were they equally  powerful but they also each wielded  their own signature weapon thor's hammer  and hercules golden mace based on what  we saw in the post-credits scene we'll  definitely see these two go head-to-head  with their respective tools of battle  and match muscles when they return to  the mcu now obviously herc's a hero so  it should be expected that the two will  eventually earn a mutual respect for one  another and join forces to stop an  actual pressing threat a threat that'll  likely scare zeus or hercules into  putting aside their vendetta just like  thor fighting tony in the first avengers  this drama between thor and herc is only  a prelude to a bromance and possibly a  new super team personally i don't see  zoo simply sending hercules after thor  on his lonesome after duking it out with  the god of thunder zeus is going to need  more than just a half mortal son after  all if gore the god butcher couldn't  take thor down with his necro sword zeus  is going to need bigger guns than the  ones attached to hercules in order to  eliminate thor some sort of suicide  squad if you will interestingly in the  comics there's actually a divine team up  known as the god squad thor himself is  part of this roster along with hercules  who leads the team this group was  originally formed to fight the skrull  gods puppeteering the events of secret  invasion as we know the mcu's version of  secret invasion featuring sam jackson's  nick fury will be coming soon-ish to  disney plus as a six-part series this is  where i believe the connective tissue  between zeus's orders in love and  thunder's post-credits scene and the  grander mcu road map connects now i'm  not saying that secret invasion will  focus on or even have cameos of thor and  her as it looks to primarily be a spy  thriller about an infiltration from an  evil sect of skrulls on earth but i do  think that the event will have some  cosmic implications that will start to  tie everything together those  implications have to do with the big g  word no not gods galactus someone who  even zeus would fear we've long  suspected that galactus might be the  mcu's next thanos level threat and this  villain absolutely ties into the comic's  secret invasion galactus destroyed the  squirrel's home world tarnox iv which  combined with their grudge against earth  superheroes propelled them to finally  infiltrate our planet this invasion was  orchestrated by the skrull gods the  deities that herc's god squad was formed  to defeat although the mcu offers a  different backstory for the skrulls  their homeworld skrellows was destroyed  by the genocidal cree and the survivors  are just trying to find their own little  slice of new asgard it would make sense  to use 2023's the marvels or secret  invasion to introduce the concept of  galactus clearly the mcu's galactus  might not be responsible for taking the  scrolls home but his cosmic energy  sucking might be affecting their ability  to find a new one i do think that if  they use either of these properties to  introduce galactus it'll be a cameo a  quick line or a post-credits scene  similar to the way that they tease  thanos in small doses pre-infinity war  in my opinion this would be a great way  for thor and hercules to end up becoming  buddies although herc could initially be  in the game to do his daddy's bidding  perhaps the upcoming events of the  marvels or secret invasion will bring  these two together in friendship just  like how they're on again off again  friends throughout the comics so if zeus  does form a team of divine beings led by  hercules to beat up thor and the events  of secret invasion are about to  influence the mcu possibly leading  towards the galactus event who could be  joining this god squad ra the egyptian  sun god is first on my list of  candidates because he was also first on  thor's short list of gods to team up  with when he landed in omnipotent city  raw was also suspiciously mia during  moon night and he could be a bridge to  bring khanshu and moon knight into the  films in irl egyptian mythology amun raz  the god of sun and light and one of the  most important deities thor's other  calls are also on the table tuma tuwanga  the maori god of war and quetzalcoatl  the aztec god of wind sun air and  learning in a perfect world i'd also  love to see a member or two from the  comics god squad added to the mcu like  snowbird and amatsu mikabashi snow bird  also known as naria is the daughter of  nilvana inuit goddess of the northern  lights and a mortal father she can  transform into any animal native to  northern canada and can also fly heal  and see into the past then we have a  matsu mikaebashi the japanese god of  chaos evil and the stars in the comics  based on a shinto god of the same name  from japanese mythology this would be a  very interesting pick for zeus's hit  team because although he technically  helped defeat nightmare in the skrull  gods and secret invasion he's still an  antagonist for hercules and thor in the  comics it would be very cool to see him  pop up in the mcu as an agent of chaos  honorable mention of course goes to bow  the god of dumplings because if anyone  could teach thor a lesson he'll never  forget it's this fearsome deity these  are just some of my predictions for who  could end up on zeus's crew but i wanna  know what you guys think in the comments  follow me on instagram and twitter  whitneypuppy follow new rockstars  subscribe to new rockstars for more  analysis of everything you love and  thanks for watching bye  [Music]  you

